This testdef is used to test variable frazil salinity coupling between
mpaso and mpassi, a stealth feature introduced by PR #8957. It sets the
following namelist options in mpaso to use porosity-based frazil salinity
and pass all of the frazil salt to the sea ice:
   config_use_frazil_ice_porosity = .true.
   config_frazil_ice_porosity = 0.85
   config_expel_excess_frazil_salt = .false.
and the following namelist options in mpassi to turn on the omega-style
frazil coupling with prognostic salt fluxes:
   config_frazil_coupling_type = 'omega-fluxes'
   config_ocean_surface_type = 'free'
   config_salt_flux_coupling_type = 'prognostic'
The mpaso settings conserve salt in the coupled system only when used with
these mpassi settings. Use this testmod with a compset that has ice-shelf
cavities and frazil under land ice (for example CRYO1850), so that frazil
salt under land ice, which is always expelled back to the ocean, is also
exercised.

The conservation check analysis members are turned on in both components:
   config_AM_conservationCheck_enable = .true.
Their energy, mass and salt budgets are written to the mpaso and mpassi
log files. Neither check aborts the run on a salt imbalance, so the logs
should be inspected to confirm conservation.
